# ALARM: Kevin Mihelich <kevin@archlinuxarm.org>
#  - let build set march on AArch64
#  - is_cfi=false, use_gold=false
#  - clang_use_default_sample_profile=false, AFDO breaks distcc
#  - disable vaapi, enable v4l2

# SmartRoom (room browser, direct V4L2 decode and encode, no VA-API):
#  - Arch Linux ARM chromium 157.0.8103.79-1 moved to 158.0.8127.36
#  - dropped chromium-149-use-of-undeclared-identifier-ERROR.patch and
#    chromium-157-crubit.patch (both already in 158)
#  - dropped chromium-157-revert-gn-check-includes.patch: 158's own pinned
#    gn (git_revision:938087829, gn 2603, linux-arm64 from CIPD) instead of
#    Arch's older gn
#  - crubit at 158's CRUBIT_REVISION
#  - sr-0001..0007: the V4L2 decode fixes and GPU sandbox change prepared
#    for upstream; sr-0008..0012: room-only encoder patches
#  - udev rule for the Apple AVD/AVE codec names
#  - use_thin_lto=false, concurrent_links=1: a ThinLTO link next to the
#    compile does not fit the 32 GB build host, which also runs a room
#  - SR_RUST_SYSROOT selects a rustup toolchain instead of pacman's rust;
#    NINJAFLAGS limits the job count

